# Compiled class file
*.class

# Log file
*.log

# BlueJ files
*.ctxt

# Mobile Tools for Java (J2ME)
.mtj.tmp/

# Package Files #
*.jar
*.war
*.nar
*.ear
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.rar

# virtual machine crash logs, see http://www.java.com/en/download/help/error_hotspot.xml
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*

# BMAD (AI-first dev framework) — the framework/tooling itself, reinstallable
# via `npx bmad-method install`. _bmad-output/ (PRD, architecture, epics,
# sprint tracking) is intentionally NOT ignored below — those are real team
# decisions/documentation, not disposable tooling output.
#
# .claude/ is per-developer local agent configuration: installed skills, editor
# launch configs, and personal permission settings. It was previously ignored
# only at .claude/skills/, which let .claude/launch.json reach the repo by
# accident in Story 8.3's PR (Epic 8 retro item 53). Widened to the whole
# directory and that file untracked — every developer's launch config points at
# their own ports and paths, so there is nothing shared to keep in version
# control.
_bmad/
.claude/

# Environment files — never commit real secrets (NFR-2). Ignore every .env*
# variant (.env, .env.local, .env.production, .env.staging, etc.) except the
# template, which documents required variables with placeholders. Order
# matters: the negation must come after the broad ignore.
.env*
!.env.example

# Backend (Maven)
backend/target/

# Frontend (Node/Vite)
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/dist-ssr/
frontend/*.local
frontend/*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
